## Goal

Two fixes. First, End turn on a finished view (`view.result !== null`) gets its own state, `over`: it reads "Game over", carries `data-turn-state="over"` (on the button and on `.turn-mechanism`), stays disabled and is sunk like the `enemy` state. That holds for a win, a loss or a draw, whoever's turn it ended on, and the opponent's live turn still reads "Enemy turn". Second, the result panel waits `resultRevealMs()` only when the effects layer plays the killing blow and Victory / Defeat. That happens only when the shown view went from no result to a result on a mounted, non-silent board. A board mounted on a finished game (Back from Watch the replay, a reload) shows `data-revealed="true"` at once. One ruling, R4734000, records both, with its paragraph in `spec/pending/4734.md`.

## Files to touch

| Path | Kind | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx` | change | `ControlButton`'s `turnState` type gains `"over"`; `endTurnState` is `"over"` on a result; End turn's `label` reads `t("Game over")` for it |
| `apps/web/src/game/board.css` | change | the `[data-turn-state="enemy"]` rule (line 2628) also selects `"over"` |
| `apps/web/src/buttons.css` | change | the `[data-turn-state="enemy"]` rule (line 123) also selects `"over"`, plus its comment |
| `apps/web/src/game/Result.tsx` | change | `GameResultProps.arrived?: boolean`; `revealMs` is `resultRevealMs()` only when `arrived`; header comment |
| `apps/web/src/game/Game.tsx` | change | state `sawLive`; passes `arrived={sawLive && !silent}` to `GameResult` |
| `apps/web/src/game/Board.test.tsx` | change | two new `R4734000` tests |
| `apps/web/src/game/Game.test.tsx` | change | rewrite "waits out the effects layer's Victory / Defeat…" to mount unfinished first; two new `R4734000` tests |
| `apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx` | change | `stubReplayFetch` gains an `opponentHere` parameter; one new `R4734000` test |
| `spec/rulings/R4734000.md` | new | the ruling note |
| `spec/pending/4734.md` | new | its §11 paragraph |

Do not touch any crate, `apps/edge`, `apps/admin`, `e2e/`, `apps/web/src/fx/` (FxLayer's timing stays as it is), `apps/web/src/practice/` (practice's own `PRACTICE_PACING.resultDelayMs`), `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md`, `spec/CARDS.md`, `spec/history/`, or anything under `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/` or `.claude/`. Do not run `cargo jackioh spec index`.

Governing: §10.10 (`spec/10-engine-guide/10.10-client-rendering.md`, the effects layer's game-over sequence), R200 (`spec/rulings/R0200.md`), R768000 (Watch the replay from the result panel), CLAUDE.md rules 3 and 7. No section text states the wait or End turn's wording, so no section is edited.

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx`, `ControlButton`'s props (line 545).** Change the type to
   `turnState?: "ready" | "waiting" | "enemy" | "locked" | "over";`

2. **`apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx`, `Board` (line 633).** Leave `ownTurn` (line 632) as it is. Replace line 633 with:
   ```ts
   // R4734000: a finished game's End turn is its own state, so it never reads Enemy turn after a game.
   const endTurnState = view.result !== null ? "over" : !ownTurn ? "enemy" : !endTurnLegal ? "locked" : actionsRemain ? "ready" : "waiting";
   ```

3. **`apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx`, End turn's `ControlButton` (line 822).** Replace the `label` prop with:
   ```tsx
   label={endTurnState === "over" ? t("Game over") : endTurnState === "enemy" ? t("Enemy turn") : armed ? t("Confirm end turn") : (endTurnLabel ?? t("End turn"))}
   ```
   `"Game over"` is already in `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json`; add no key.

4. **`apps/web/src/game/board.css`, line 2628.** Make the rule's selector a list, body unchanged:
   ```css
   .board .control.control-end-turn[data-turn-state="enemy"],
   .board .control.control-end-turn[data-turn-state="over"] {
   ```

5. **`apps/web/src/buttons.css`, line 123.** Do the same to the `enemy` rule (its border, sunken background and dimmed text), body unchanged. Change its comment's first line (line 121) to `/* End turn in the opponent's turn and after the game (R4734000): its housing sunk into the rail and dimmed (board.css draws the`. Without this the `over` button would get the disabled primary's face, not the `enemy` one.

6. **`apps/web/src/game/Result.tsx`, `GameResultProps` (lines 127-143).** Add as the last member:
   ```ts
   /**
    * R4734000: whether the result arrived on the mounted board: its shown view went from no result to one,
    * the change the effects layer plays the killing blow and Victory / Defeat on. Only then does the panel
    * wait `resultRevealMs()`; absent or false, it comes in at once, since nothing plays.
    */
   arrived?: boolean;
   ```
   - In `GameResult`'s destructuring (after `openResultTestId,`) add `arrived = false,`.
   - Replace line 161 with `const [revealMs] = useState(() => (arrived ? resultRevealMs() : 0));`.
   - In the file header, change lines 6-7's "Both wait for the effects layer's Victory / Defeat sequence (`revealMs`) instead of sitting under its word," to "Both wait for the effects layer's Victory / Defeat sequence (`revealMs`) instead of sitting under its word, when it plays: only a result that arrived on the mounted board (`arrived`, R4734000) waits;".
   - Leave `resultRevealMs()` itself unchanged.

7. **`apps/web/src/game/Game.tsx`, below `latest.current = view;` (line 418).** Add:
   ```ts
   // R4734000: whether this board has shown the game unfinished. The effects layer plays the killing blow and
   // Victory / Defeat only when the shown view goes from no result to one on a mounted board (FxLayer.tsx), and
   // a silent board has no effects layer, so only then does the result wait for them (`GameResult`'s `arrived`).
   // A board mounted on a finished game (Back from Watch the replay, a reload) shows its result at once. React's
   // "adjust state while rendering" pattern, as the concede dialog below does.
   const [sawLive, setSawLive] = useState(view.result === null);
   if (!sawLive && shown.result === null) setSawLive(true);
   ```
   In the `<GameResult …>` element (around line 1164), add `arrived={sawLive && !silent}` after `openResultTestId={openResultTestId}`. `silent` is already a destructured prop (line 353).

8. **Write the tests** in the **Tests** section below, then the ruling (steps 9-10).

9. **`spec/rulings/R4734000.md`** (new):
   ```markdown
   ---
   id: R4734000
   title: "A finished game's End turn reads Game over, and its result waits for Victory / Defeat only when they play (issue #4734)"
   cards: "§10.10, R200, R768000, issue #4734"
   proven_in:
     - apps/web/src/game/Board.test.tsx
     - apps/web/src/game/Game.test.tsx
     - apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx
   ---

   Not a rule of the game (CLAUDE.md rule 7): what the board shows once the view carries a result.

   **End turn after the game.** A view with a result gives End turn its own state, `over`
   (`data-turn-state="over"` on the button and its `.turn-mechanism`): it reads "Game over", the turn
   plate's word, stays disabled as no move is legal, and is sunk and dimmed as in the opponent's turn
   (`game/board.css`, `buttons.css`). This holds for a win, a loss and a draw, whoever's turn the game ended
   on; before, every finished view read "Enemy turn", the only turn wording on a phone held upright. The
   opponent's live turn still reads "Enemy turn". Hiding End turn instead was rejected: the rail's layout
   would shift as the result comes in.

   **The result waits only for what plays.** The effects layer plays the killing blow and Victory / Defeat
   ([[§10.10]], [[R200]]) only when the shown view goes from no result to one on a board that is already
   mounted, and a silent board (the co-op teammate's) has no effects layer. So the result panel or chip
   waits `resultRevealMs()` (`FX_LETHAL_LEAD_MAX_MS` + `FX_RESULT_MS`) only on a board that showed the game
   unfinished and is not silent (`Game`'s `arrived`). A board mounted on a finished game, such as the one
   Back from Watch the replay ([[R768000]]) or a reload mounts, shows its result with `data-revealed="true"`
   at once, Rematch included; before, it stayed transparent and took no pointer for 3.8 s waiting on an
   animation that never played. Reduced motion and effects off wait for nothing, as before.
   ```

10. **`spec/pending/4734.md`** (new, one line; the date is the day you write it):
    ```markdown
    **[[R4734000]] A finished game's End turn reads Game over, and its result waits for Victory / Defeat only when they play (issue #4734, 2026-11-25)**: asked by issue #4734, which found End turn reading "Enemy turn" after every game and a board mounted on a finished game (Back from Watch the replay) hiding its result for 3.8 s. Edits no section. Takes R4734000.
    ```

## Tests

**`apps/web/src/game/Board.test.tsx`**: add these after "builds End turn into its rail and reflects existing legality without deciding a move". That test stays unchanged and still covers "Enemy turn".
```tsx
it("R4734000 a finished view's End turn reads Game over, carries data-turn-state over and stays disabled", () => {
  const view = fullBoardView();
  const results: NonNullable<PlayerView["result"]>[] = [
    { winner: view.viewer, reason: "hero-death" },
    { winner: view.opponent.player, reason: "hero-death" },
    { winner: "draw", reason: "draw-accepted" },
  ];
  for (const result of results) {
    for (const active of [view.viewer, view.opponent.player]) {
      const board = render(<Board view={{ ...view, active, result }} highlight={NO_HIGHLIGHT} />);
      const endTurn = screen.getByTestId(testid.endTurn);
      const what = `${result.winner} won, ${active} active`;
      expect(endTurn, what).toHaveTextContent("Game over");
      expect(endTurn, what).not.toHaveTextContent("Enemy turn");
      expect(endTurn.getAttribute("data-turn-state"), what).toBe("over");
      expect(endTurn.closest(".turn-mechanism")?.getAttribute("data-turn-state"), what).toBe("over");
      expect(endTurn, what).toBeDisabled();
      board.unmount();
    }
  }
});

it("R4734000 Game over's End turn is sunk as the opponent's turn is", () => {
  const buttonsCss = readFileSync(join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), "..", "buttons.css"), "utf8");
  const pair = '.board .control.control-end-turn[data-turn-state="enemy"], .board .control.control-end-turn[data-turn-state="over"] {';
  expect(boardCss.replace(/\s+/g, " ")).toContain(pair);
  expect(buttonsCss.replace(/\s+/g, " ")).toContain(pair);
});
```
`readFileSync`, `join`, `dirname`, `fileURLToPath`, `PlayerView`, `NO_HIGHLIGHT` and `boardCss` are already in scope.

**`apps/web/src/game/Game.test.tsx`**, in `describe("the result overlay")`:
- Rewrite "waits out the effects layer's Victory / Defeat before it takes the pointer" (line 344), keeping its name. Its first line becomes `const { rerender } = render(<Game view={baseView()} legal={[]} onAction={vi.fn()} />);`, followed by `rerender(<Game view={finished()} legal={[]} onAction={vi.fn()} />);`. The rest is unchanged: `data-revealed="false"`, a non-empty `animationDelay`, then `"true"` after 10 s.
- Add `it("R4734000 a board mounted on a finished game shows its result at once, with no animation delay")`. It renders `render(<Game view={finished()} legal={[]} onAction={vi.fn()} />)` and advances no timer. Then:
  - the overlay has `data-revealed="true"`;
  - `expect(overlay.style.animationDelay).toBe("")`;
  - `expect(document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".result-scrim")?.style.animationDelay).toBe("")`.
- Add `it("R4734000 a silent board's result waits for nothing: no effects layer plays on it")`. It renders `const { rerender } = render(<Game view={baseView()} legal={[]} onAction={vi.fn()} silent />)`, then `rerender(<Game view={finished()} legal={[]} onAction={vi.fn()} silent />)`, and the overlay has `data-revealed="true"`.

**`apps/web/src/routes/match.test.tsx`**:
- Leave `#1664 plays the tracks…` (line 1162) unchanged. Its `attach()` already pushes an unfinished `baseView({ viewer: "p1", active: "p1" })` before `push(finished)`, so the board mounts live and still waits. The issue's "pushes finished as its first view" is wrong about this. If the test fails anyway, add `push(baseView({ viewer: "p1", active: "p1" }));` before its first `push(finished);` and say so in your report.
- In `describe("R768000 a finished match's replay from its result panel")`, change `stubReplayFetch` (line 1779) to `function stubReplayFetch(ranks?: unknown, pages: "served" | "pending" = "served", opponentHere = false): string[]`, and its `/rematch` body to `{ youOffered: null, opponentOffer: null, opponentHere, matchId: null }`. Existing callers stay as they are.
- Add after "R768000 Watch the replay loads…":
  ```tsx
  it("R4734000 after Watch the replay and Back, the result and its Rematch are in with no wait", async () => {
    stubReplayFetch(undefined, "served", true);
    render(<MatchRoute matchId="m-1" token="tok" socketFactory={socketFactory} />);
    attach();
    pushView(baseView({ viewer: "p1", active: "p1", result: { winner: "p1", reason: "hero-death" } }));
    // The result arrived on the mounted board: it waits for the effects layer's Victory.
    expect(screen.getByTestId("result-overlay")).toHaveAttribute("data-revealed", "false");

    fireEvent.click(await screen.findByTestId(matchTestid.watchReplay));
    await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByTestId(replayTestid.player)).toHaveAttribute("data-step", "0"));
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByTestId(replayTestid.back));

    // Back mounts a fresh board on the finished game: nothing plays, so nothing is waited for.
    expect(await screen.findByTestId("rematch-offer")).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByTestId("result-overlay")).toHaveAttribute("data-revealed", "true");
    expect(screen.getByTestId("result-overlay").style.animationDelay).toBe("");
  });
  ```
  This suite runs on real timers, so the 3.8 s wait cannot finish inside `findBy`'s 1 s, and the test fails without the fix.

